---
/**
 * Close Contact's dedicated FAQ (moved off the homepage, which now carries only general/brand
 * questions — see GeneralFaq.astro). Several answers make body/attraction/ingredient claims (same
 * category as the flagged copy elsewhere on this page), so they carry data-copy-review, same
 * convention as the rest of the site. No FAQPage JSON-LD is added here — see docs/faq-proposal.md,
 * still pending approval.
 */
import ProductFaqGroup from '@/components/product/ProductFaqGroup.astro';
import Brand from '@/components/ui/Brand.astro';

const item = 'border-b-2 border-dashed border-green';
const question = 'flex min-h-12 items-center justify-between gap-5 py-6 text-[clamp(1.15rem,2vw,1.5rem)] font-black uppercase';
const plus = 'faq-plus flex-none text-[26px] font-black';
const answer = 'max-w-[60ch] pb-6 text-[19px] leading-[1.55]';
---

<section id="faq" class="section-px section-py bg-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[900px]">
    <h2 class="display-word stretch-display text-[clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4.25rem)] leading-[0.88]">Close Contact, answered</h2>

    <div class="mt-[clamp(40px,5vw,64px)]">
      <ProductFaqGroup badgeClass="bg-pink text-ink">
        <span slot="badge">Close Contact</span>

        <details name="faq-close-contact" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>
              What is <Brand /> Close Contact?
            </span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            <strong>Close Contact is a chewable dietary supplement designed to support your body's natural chemistry from within</strong>. It combines functional ingredients with a <strong>pineapple flavor</strong> and a <strong>liquid center</strong> —
            because taking a supplement shouldn't feel like taking a supplement.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-close-contact" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>How does Close Contact work?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            <strong>Close Contact is designed to complement the processes that influence how your body smells and tastes up close</strong>. Instead of masking your natural chemistry with fragrance, it provides nutritional support from within.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-close-contact" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Can Close Contact change how I smell?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            Your natural scent is influenced by many things, including food, metabolism, skin and sweat.
            <strong>Close Contact is designed to support that internal chemistry</strong> — not replace deodorant, perfume or good
            hygiene.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-close-contact" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Can Close Contact affect how body fluids taste?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]} data-copy-review="PENDING: wording already matches Notion Regulatory & Compliance §3's conservative guidance verbatim; keep flagged for final legal sign-off given the sensitive subject matter, not because the wording itself is non-compliant">
            Body fluids have their own chemistry, and what you eat can contribute to that chemistry.
            <strong>Close Contact is designed around this idea</strong>, but we do not claim that it directly changes the taste of
            <strong>semen</strong>, <strong>vaginal fluids</strong> or other specific <strong>body fluids</strong> unless
            supported by product-specific clinical evidence.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-close-contact" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Is Close Contact a breath mint, gum or candy?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            None of the above. <strong>Close Contact is a chewable dietary supplement with a gummy texture and liquid center</strong>.
            It isn't designed simply to make your mouth taste like pineapple.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-close-contact" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>What ingredients are in Close Contact?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            The formula includes zinc, maca and L-arginine, together with the ingredients needed to create the gummy and
            liquid-center format. The final Supplement Facts panel will always be the definitive source for the complete
            formula and amounts.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-close-contact" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Why does Close Contact contain zinc?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]} data-copy-review="PENDING (see Notion Regulatory & Compliance §3): already correctly hedged (defers to final dose), keep flagged until that dose is confirmed">
            Zinc is an essential mineral involved in numerous normal functions in the body, including normal metabolism,
            maintenance of normal skin and normal taste perception. The amount in <strong>Close Contact</strong> will determine
            which specific nutrient claims can legally be made for the finished product.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-close-contact" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Does Close Contact replace a healthy diet?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            No. Dietary supplements are intended to supplement the diet, not replace a varied and balanced diet.
            <strong>Close Contact is the little extra</strong> — not an excuse to make fries your food group.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-close-contact" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>What does Close Contact taste like?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            <strong>Bright, juicy pineapple with a soft gummy bite — and a liquid center that pops when you chew</strong>. It
            starts fruity, finishes fresh and leaves you with that little "okay, what was that?" moment.
            <strong>It's not gum. It's not candy. It's <Brand /> Close Contact</strong>.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-close-contact" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>How many Close Contact gummies should I take?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            <strong>We recommend 1–3 gummies per day, preferably after a meal</strong>. Start with one and find what works for
            you — without exceeding the recommended daily serving on the package.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details name="faq-close-contact" class:list={[item]}>
          <summary class:list={[question]}>
            <span>Is Close Contact safe?</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true" class:list={[plus]}>+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class:list={[answer]}>
            <strong>Close Contact</strong> will be formulated and manufactured as a dietary supplement according to the
            requirements applicable to its launch market. Follow the <a href="#whats-inside">serving size</a> and speak with a
            healthcare professional if you have a medical condition, are pregnant or breastfeeding, or take medications.
          </p>
        </details>
      </ProductFaqGroup>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
